2. Execution Flow Freeze
UI Component
      │
React Query Hook
      │
Frontend API
      │
HTTP
      │
Route Handler
(Auth + Validation)
      │
Service
(Business Logic)
      │
Repository
(Database)
      │
Drizzle
      │
PostgreSQL

No shortcuts.

Repositories never call HTTP.

Services never know about Route Handlers.

Route Handlers never contain business logic.

3. Responsibilities Freeze
UI → Rendering only
Hook → Server state only
API → Network communication only
Route → Auth, validation, response
Service → Business rules
Repository → Data access only
4. DTO Strategy Freeze

DTOs represent UI requirements, not database tables.

They:

hide database implementation
combine fields where needed
expose only what the frontend needs
are exported through index.ts
5. Mapper Strategy Freeze

Mappers are the only place that converts between:

Database Entity → DTO
DTO → Repository Input

No conversion logic in Services or UI.

6. React Query Strategy Freeze

Every server interaction gets:

Query Key
API Client
Hook

Pattern:

keys.ts
↓

api/

↓

hooks/

No component calls fetch() directly.

7. Validation Strategy Freeze

Validation occurs twice:

Frontend:

React Hook Form
Zod

Backend:

Route Handler
Same schema (or shared schema where appropriate)
8. Error Strategy Freeze

One unified response format.

Validation errors

↓

Business errors

↓

Database errors

↓

Unexpected errors

Everything returns through common response helpers.

9. State Strategy Freeze

Server State

→ React Query

Local Form State

→ React Hook Form

UI State

→ React state

No duplicated state.

10. File Upload Strategy Freeze

Media uploads will be isolated into their own module.

Responsibilities:

upload
reorder
delete
cover image
validation
optimization
